		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2028#p2028"><![CDATA[
1) You Draw N polygons. Each polygon consists of N pixels. Right?<br>2) Your render target texture contains only N pixels. Or N*N?<br>3) If N*N then I do not understand why you need second pass...<br><br>For example, in my approach I draw only ONE triangle. Triangle cathetus are N-1 pixels. Area: (N^2-N)/2. This triangle contains all collisions. And I do not use vertex shader at all.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=772">Jack</a> — Tue Oct 03, 2006 7:10 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
